3
00:00:15.861 --> 00:00:28.192
<v NARRATOR>On a smooth grey stone at the edge of a slow stream, a thousand tiny builders were laying down a roof, and Colony was right in the thick of it.

4
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:39.043
<v NARRATOR>You could not see Colony as one thing — Colony was a warm coral-and-gold cluster of many small rounds, all linked shoulder to shoulder.

5
00:00:39.043 --> 00:00:50.174
<v COLONY>We are a biofilm — a whole city of single cells, anchored to this stone and sheltering under one roof we built out of ourselves.

6
00:00:50.174 --> 00:00:59.785
<v NARRATOR>A single microbe came drifting down the current, spinning and thin, and clung to the stone, trembling.

7
00:00:59.785 --> 00:01:08.756
<v COLONY>Come in, little one, there is always room — a community that only kept its strongest would stay small and brittle forever.

8
00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:16.447
<v NARRATOR>The cluster shuffled sideways and made a gap, and the trembling speck settled in among them.

9
00:01:16.447 --> 00:01:25.978
<v COLONY>Alone, a single cell is almost nothing — one current could tumble it away, one dry hour could end it entirely.

10
00:01:25.978 --> 00:01:38.229
<v COLONY>So we ooze a shared slime, a matrix of sugars and proteins, and it glues us together and keeps the water in and the poisons out.

11
00:01:38.229 --> 00:01:45.560
<v NARRATOR>The cells passed food hand to hand, and sent chemical signals so they could act as one.

12
00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:55.251
<v COLONY>We can even sense how many of us have gathered — and only when enough of us have arrived do we all switch on the building at once.

13
00:01:55.251 --> 00:02:05.262
<v NARRATOR>The same trick makes the plaque on your teeth, the slick films on plant roots, and the mats that hold a whole meadow's soil together.

14
00:02:05.262 --> 00:02:14.913
<v COLONY>A single cell is a piece the roof cannot be built without, so every one who clings on is one more reason the whole thing holds.

15
00:02:14.913 --> 00:02:26.124
<v NARRATOR>Many fragile singles, pooling what little each can spare, become one durable whole. That is what makes Colony a city.

16
